  "worked_solution": "To get $a$ and $b$, we need to find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y=3-{x}^{2}.$ \n\nWe solve the equation for $y=0$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-\\sqrt{3}$ and $b=\\sqrt{3}.$",
